  {
   "slug": "science-fair-winners",
   "title": "Meet This Year's Science Fair Winners",
   "date": "2026-09-28T14:00:00",
   "excerpt": "A water filter made from sand and charcoal, a bee-friendly balcony and a very determined robot. Congratulations to all forty entries.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The main hall was packed on Friday for our annual science fair. Forty projects, three judges, and more cardboard than anyone thought possible.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">First place</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A gravity-fed water filter built from sand, gravel and charcoal, tested for a whole month.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Second place</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A balcony garden designed to attract bees, with a careful count of every visitor.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Judges' prize</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A line-following robot that refused to give up, even when the line ran out.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The best projects were the ones where something went wrong and the students explained why.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Head of Science</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>All projects will be on display in the library until the end of the month. Come and see them.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:gallery {\"columns\":3,\"linkTo\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped\"><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:science}}\" alt=\"Science fair projects on tables\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:lab}}\" alt=\"Glassware and plants in the lab\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:library}}\" alt=\"The library reading room\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --></figure><!-- /wp:gallery -->",
   "categories": [
    "student-life"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "science",
    "awards"
   ],
   "featured_media": "science",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "open-evening-november",
   "title": "Open Evening: Visit the Commons on 14 November",
   "date": "2026-09-15T10:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Tour the classrooms, meet the teachers and try a ten-minute taster class. Everyone is welcome, no booking needed.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Thinking about joining us? Our autumn open evening is the best way to see what learning at the Commons feels like.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:table --><figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>What is happening</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>17:30</td><td>Doors open, welcome in the main hall</td></tr><tr><td>18:00</td><td>Taster classes (ten minutes each, try as many as you like)</td></tr><tr><td>19:00</td><td>Talk: how our courses work</td></tr><tr><td>19:30</td><td>Questions and tea with the teachers</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><!-- /wp:table --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The building is step-free and there is free parking behind the library. Children are very welcome.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"{{page:events}}\">All events</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Can't make it on the night? Our front office runs short guided tours every Wednesday afternoon during term time.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "events"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "open-evening",
    "admissions"
   ],
   "featured_media": "campus",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "five-tips-for-learning-a-language-as-an-adult",
   "title": "Five Tips for Learning a Language as an Adult",
   "date": "2026-09-02T08:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Our languages team shares what actually works for adult learners, from ten-minute habits to the courage to sound silly.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Adults are excellent language learners. You bring discipline, life experience and a clear reason to learn. What you often lack is permission to make mistakes.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Little and often beats long and rare.</strong> Ten minutes a day is better than two hours on Sunday.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Speak from week one.</strong> Even badly. Especially badly.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Learn phrases, not just words.</strong> \"Could I have…\" is more useful than \"cup\".</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Listen to things you enjoy.</strong> Cooking shows, football, music.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Find a partner.</strong> Our conversation café meets every Wednesday.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>You do not need a talent for languages. You need a habit.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Languages coordinator</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our spring languages courses include Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, German and Japanese, at four levels each.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "courses",
    "student-life"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "languages",
    "study-skills"
   ],
   "featured_media": "languages",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "new-glasshouse-classroom",
   "title": "Our New Glasshouse Classroom Is Finished",
   "date": "2026-08-20T11:00:00",
   "excerpt": "After two years of fundraising and one long summer of building, the glasshouse classroom is ready for its first students.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>It started as a rough sketch on a staff-room whiteboard. Now it is a bright glass classroom with room for twenty-four students, a rainwater tank and benches made from the old gym floor.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaType\":\"image\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"{{media:lab}}\" alt=\"Plants and glassware in the glasshouse\" class=\"size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What happens here</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Botany and biology practicals</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>The gardening club</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Evening talks in summer</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div></div><!-- /wp:media-text --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Thank you to the 300 families and local businesses who donated. Every name is on the plaque by the door.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The first classes in the glasshouse begin in the spring term, starting with Introduction to Botany on Thursday mornings.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "news"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "campus",
    "science"
   ],
   "featured_media": "lab",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Jon",
     "email": "jon@example.com",
     "content": "Beautiful space. The gym-floor benches are a lovely touch.",
     "date": "2026-08-21T16:30:00"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "welcome-to-our-new-teachers",
   "title": "Welcome to Our New Teachers",
   "date": "2026-08-05T09:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Three new teachers join the Commons this term, bringing botany, woodwork and Portuguese to the timetable.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Every new term brings new faces, and this one brings three. Please give them a warm welcome when you see them in the corridors.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:teacher-1}}\" alt=\"Abstract portrait illustration of a teacher\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ms. Hana Brightwater</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Botany and biology. Has never met a plant she could not name.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:teacher-2}}\" alt=\"Abstract portrait illustration of a teacher\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Mr. Tomas Ferreira</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Portuguese and Spanish. Teaches with music, food and maps.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:teacher-3}}\" alt=\"Abstract portrait illustration of a teacher\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Mx. Robin Ashby</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Woodwork. Believes every student can make a chair.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>You can find all our staff on the faculty page.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "faculty"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "staff"
   ],
   "featured_media": "faculty",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "study-spaces-guide",
   "title": "A Guide to Quiet Study Spaces on Campus",
   "date": "2026-07-18T13:00:00",
   "excerpt": "From the silent reading room to the sunny bench behind the workshop, here is where to go when you need to concentrate.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Everyone studies differently. Some people need silence; others need a little background noise and a window. We asked students for their favourite spots.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>The reading room</strong>: silent, bright, open until 21:00.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>The group rooms</strong>: bookable for up to six people.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>The glasshouse</strong>: warm and green, quiet outside class times.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>The bench behind the workshop</strong>: the best-kept secret on campus.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Wi-Fi is available everywhere. Power sockets are, sadly, a different story; the reading room has the most.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Know a better spot? Tell us at the front office and we may add it to next year's guide.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "student-life"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "study-skills",
    "campus"
   ],
   "featured_media": "study",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "summer-school-recap",
   "title": "Summer School in Pictures",
   "date": "2026-07-02T16:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Two weeks, 180 students, 14 workshops and one unforgettable water-rocket launch. A look back at this year's summer school.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Summer school is always the loudest, happiest fortnight of the year. This year we tried something new: every workshop ended with something to take home.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:gallery {\"columns\":3,\"linkTo\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped\"><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:science}}\" alt=\"Students&#x27; science projects\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:art}}\" alt=\"Paint and paper in the art studio\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:campus}}\" alt=\"The campus lawn in summer\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --></figure><!-- /wp:gallery --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Highlights included a water-rocket launch that reached the library roof, a poetry slam in the courtyard and a cooking class that set off exactly one smoke alarm.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>I came for the robots and stayed for the poetry.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>A summer school student</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->",
   "categories": [
    "events",
    "student-life"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "summer-school"
   ],
   "featured_media": "campus",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  }
 ],
